        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Full main Theorem3.14 with the existence1.5, integrability Proposition1.3 and complete uniqueness Theorem3.9 proofs is supplied. The base Sigma is connected; omega:A->g satisfies M1 transitivity, M2 isotropy injectivity at a point and M3 isotropy inclusion into an action stabilizer. Existence requires the pointed monodromy to be constant. Uniqueness up to the author Definition3.1 homogeneous-space symmetries additionally requires maximal rank and weakly connected isotropy, meaning equality of the two normalizers N_G(H)=N_G(H^0), not ordinary connected stabilizers. Lie I/II and the established Crainic-Fernandes integrability criterion are background; the new global construction and normalizer comparison are shown. Preserve the source local notation slips in1.8 and the concluding3.12 proof literally, with the warning below; the preceding construction and Proposition3.12 statement explicitly specify the relevant maps, so no new argument is supplied."
      },
